+# ADR-0014: JSON Library Policy
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+GoModel uses three JSON libraries and one YAML library. Each does a different
+job, but the rule for choosing between them was written nowhere, so new code
+copied whatever the neighbouring file did. That already produced three copies
+of the same `[]string` column helper split across two JSON libraries, and a
+stdlib import justified by a reason that does not hold.
+
+| Library | Job |
+|---------|-----|
+| `github.com/goccy/go-json` | Default marshal/unmarshal, including echo's response serializer (`internal/server/json_serializer.go`) |
+| `github.com/tidwall/gjson` | Read-only path queries over raw bytes, without unmarshalling |
+| `encoding/json` | Sites that need the standard library's exact semantics |
+| `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` | `config.yaml` |
+
+## Decision
+
+1. **goccy by default.** Import `github.com/goccy/go-json` as `json` for
+   marshal, unmarshal, encoders and decoders. It is on the hot path and the
+   pre-commit `make perf-check` guard measures it.
+2. **gjson for read-only extraction.** When code only needs a few values from
+   raw bytes (selector peek, session detection, cache keys, upstream error
+   bodies), use `gjson` instead of decoding into a struct or map. goccy has no
+   equivalent API.
+3. **`encoding/json` only where its exact semantics are required**, and the
+   import says which semantics and why, in a comment next to it. Current
+   reasons:
+   - `pluginapi` must depend on the standard library only (`TestStdlibOnly`).
+   - echo's binder (`DefaultJSONSerializer.Deserialize`) is stdlib.
+   - `config/merge.go` uses the stdlib streaming decoder to reject unknown
+     fields and trailing data in JSON env vars.
+   - `internal/server/messages_native.go` splices bytes using the stdlib
+     decoder's documented `RawMessage` and `InputOffset` behaviour.
+   - `internal/auditlog/body.go` uses stdlib `Valid`, a strict allocation-free
+     scan, where goccy's `Valid` decodes the document.
+4. **`yaml.v3` only for YAML config.**
+5. **Shared column helpers live in `internal/storage/sqlutil`.** A JSON
+   `[]string` column uses `EncodeJSONStrings`/`DecodeJSONStrings` (`NOT NULL`,
+   errors returned) or `NullableJSONStrings`/`StringsFromJSON` (nullable,
+   malformed rows logged and skipped) instead of a store-local copy.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- New code has one rule to follow, and reviewers have one place to point to.
+- Older `encoding/json` imports that do not state a reason predate this ADR.
+  When touching one, add the reason or switch it to goccy.
+- No dependency is added or removed.
